CSS isn't loading via document.write(). This is a limitation of the current world.js approach. So the computed style won't reflect the CSS rules from the external files. The step definition needs to check the CSS-based visibility via a different mechanism.

Since the app uses the `editing` class on the li element to control visibility via CSS, and the CSS isn't loaded in happy-dom, I need to either:
